    {
      "source": "Road Trail Run",
      "priority": 4,
      "url": "https://www.roadtrailrun.com/2025/11/puma-magmax-nitro-2-review-4-comparisons.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: Very soft, highly cushioned ride from the 46 mm heel / 38 mm forefoot Nitro foam stack, with strong impact protection and a plush heel-to-forefoot feel plus some forefoot flex.",
        "Responsiveness: Bounce is high but energy return is only moderate; the ride is described as not particularly quick to return energy and lacking decisive pop/snappiness at faster paces.",
        "Stability: Stability is the main weakness, with a soft high stack, narrow 75 mm midfoot, less-than-rigid heel counter, and limited rear/midfoot outsole support causing slight wobble and side rotation on landings.",
        "Durability: Outsole durability is a positive via PumaGrip (called high-performing and durable), but the sparse rubber layout (two rear patches and forefoot strips) prioritizes low weight and may limit long-term structural support."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Believe in the Run",
      "priority": 5,
      "url": "https://believeintherun.com/shoe-reviews/puma-magmax-nitro-2-review/",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The 46/38 mm NitroFoam setup feels plush and soft with strong impact protection, with reviewers noting v2 is slightly softer and more resilient than v1 across heel-to-forefoot landings.",
        "Responsiveness: NitroFoam adds noticeable rebound/energy return, giving a bouncy, snappy-enough ride that handled easy runs through moderate uptempo sections (but not true speed-session focus).",
        "Stability: A wide, stable platform, secure upper lockdown, and a less bulbous forefoot improved lateral support and overall control for a neutral max-cushion shoe; mild overpronation was tolerated, while severe overpronators may need more guidance.",
        "Durability: PumaGrip outsole traction stayed reliable even on post-snow/icy patches, and reviewers called overall shoe durability/material longevity exceptional for the price."
      ]
    }
